WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:04.280
One of the more confusing aspects of The Nun
is the fact that Valak is constantly manipulating

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:07.790
things, and it’s hard for us as an audience
to get a grip on what’s real and what’s

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:08.790
not.

00:00:08.790 --> 00:00:12.210
For the ultimate guide on what exists and
what is just an apparition, stick around to

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:13.380
the end of this video.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:20.990
I know what you’re probably thinking, “Oh
it’s this guy who jumpscared us, let’s

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:22.019
lock him up forever.”

00:00:22.019 --> 00:00:25.849
Look, this video’s not about the jumpscares,
it’s about Things You Missed In The Nun.

00:00:25.849 --> 00:00:29.460
Now, I do reserve the right to jumpscare at
any time during my videos, but I don’t usually

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:35.090
pull it out for Things You Missed; all I can
say is to stay on your toes, and let’s get

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:36.420
into it.

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:40.039
Like I pointed out when I made this video,
in The Conjuring 2, the name of the Nun demon

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:43.160
Valak is hidden within many of the scenes
like so…

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:45.070
And that trend continues here in The Nun.

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:48.980
For example, when we first meet Sister Irene
at the religious school she teaches at, when

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:52.090
they show the playground, there is a see-saw
that some kids are playing on.

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:55.579
The bars that makeup the supports of the see-saw
spell out the word Valak.

00:00:55.579 --> 00:01:00.160
Then, in Biertan, the Romanian town near The
Abbey, Frenchie has Sister Irene and Father

00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:01.910
Burke load their stuff onto a truck.

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:05.890
The license plate of the truck reads VA 01
LAK.

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:08.250
If you remove the numbers, it spells out Valak.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:12.210
There’s also a crossword puzzle that Father
Burke is seen solving a couple different times

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:13.210
in the film.

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:16.810
Take a look at some of the boxes he’s written
in and you’ll see the words Deliveries and

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:17.810
Create.

00:01:17.810 --> 00:01:20.680
I bet you thought I was going to say that
it said Valak, but the fact of the matter

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:24.140
is that the shots weren’t on screen long
enough for me to see everything, so if you

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:28.189
saw anything pertaining to Valak or anything
of significance at all, leave a comment telling

00:01:28.189 --> 00:01:31.600
me what you saw, and I’ll pin your comment,
and you’ll be famous and it will be a great

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:32.649
day for you.

00:01:32.649 --> 00:01:35.979
So… remember when I did that one video where
I explained the deeper meaning behind the

00:01:35.979 --> 00:01:38.600
song that comes on the radio in the commercial
for The Nun?

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:42.310
Well… it may have been all for nothing,
because the song that comes on in the actual

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:43.720
movie is different.

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:48.170
“Just remember darling all the while.

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:57.280
You belong to me.”

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:00.350
The song is You Belong To Me, performed by
Jo Stafford.

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:03.479
Like the song that was used in the commercial,
it’s a cover of an existing song from that

00:02:03.479 --> 00:02:04.479
era.

00:02:04.479 --> 00:02:08.319
In this case, the song is used as a direct
message from Valak to Father Burke, a warning

00:02:08.319 --> 00:02:10.570
that if he stays in The Abbey, he’s in for
trouble.

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:14.730
Valak is literally telling him, “you belong
to me now” and it’s a foreshadow of the

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:17.660
scene where the Father is locked in a coffin
where Valak tortures him.

00:02:17.660 --> 00:02:21.349
It sure was nice of Valak to leave that shovel
there for Sister Irene when she eventually

00:02:21.349 --> 00:02:22.640
does find the father.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:26.080
While she’s looking for him though, Valak
lures her into the chapel, where a couple

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.700
of interesting things happen.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:31.220
First off, the Nuns are chanting, so she should
immediately know that something is up, because

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:34.040
we were just told they are taking a vow of
silence.

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:37.720
Then Sister Irene sees a red glowing light
coming up from below the altar, a symbol of

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.610
the fires of hell manifesting in the Abbey.

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:43.630
At this point, she follows the shadow of The
Nun along wall, landing on the mirror behind

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:47.140
her, where it is revealed that Valak is standing
above her, however, the figure can only be

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:48.690
seen in the reflection.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:52.800
Later on, when Frenchie is at the Black Bear
pub back in town, he notices a woman covering

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:53.800
up a mirror.

00:02:53.800 --> 00:02:56.940
When he asks about it, the bartender tells
him that a young girl had recently died, and

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:01.099
that it was a tradition in town to cover up
mirrors so that the deceased do not see their

00:03:01.099 --> 00:03:02.099
own reflection.

00:03:02.099 --> 00:03:06.349
Remember the photo that Sister Charlotte shows
from her time in Romania in Annabelle Creation?

00:03:06.349 --> 00:03:09.700
I had previously speculated that we would
meet some of the characters from the photo

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:14.750
in The Nun, however, Sister Maria, Sister
Anna and Sister Lucia do not appear.

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:18.310
This is because Sister Charlotte visited the
Abbey before the events of The Nun took place.

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:21.780
You can actually spot this same photo on the
wall when they come into the Abbey.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:25.100
Poor Sister Charlotte has no idea that her
friends are all dead.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:29.439
Another item I speculated on was the relationship
between Sister Irene from The Nun, and Lorraine

00:03:29.439 --> 00:03:30.939
Warren from The Conjuring films.

00:03:30.939 --> 00:03:35.290
I thought they might be sisters because they
both have visions of Valak and the actresses

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:37.239
who play them are sisters in real life.

00:03:37.239 --> 00:03:41.099
In The Nun, no relationship is confirmed,
however, I do find it interesting that The

00:03:41.099 --> 00:03:45.210
Vatican selected Sister Irene to accompany
the Father, despite the fact that she is unfamiliar

00:03:45.210 --> 00:03:46.210
with the area.

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:49.250
The Father mentions that The Vatican always
has a reason for their selection, so I think

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:52.569
it’s still possible that the two are related
in some way, and that has something to do

00:03:52.569 --> 00:03:53.970
with why she was sent.

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:57.570
While we don’t get much background on Sister
Irene, we do get a little bit more background

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:58.570
on Valak.

00:03:58.570 --> 00:04:02.659
Father Burke researches to find that The Abbey
was built by a Duke who wrote books and opened

00:04:02.659 --> 00:04:03.870
a gateway to hell.

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:07.220
This information may be a nod to the fact
that Valak is based off a character from a

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:12.180
book called The Lesser Key of Solomon, which
I have gone into more detail on in this video.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:16.360
The Gateway was sealed with the blood of Christ,
but reopened later due to a war of some kind.

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:20.390
Valak appears as a Nun in order to blend in
with the real Nuns that that reside at the

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:24.380
Abbey, so my theory about Valak possibly changing
forms has gained a little more weight.

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:27.610
The other thing I pointed out in my previous
video about the pages of the book was this

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:30.800
illustration, which appears to be a snake
coming out of someone’s face.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:33.970
The idea of a snake being another form of
Valak is confirmed in The Nun.

00:04:33.970 --> 00:04:37.490
Father Burke reads a description of Valak
in the book that he finds inside his coffin,

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:41.820
which reads, “Valak, the defiler, the profane,
the marquis of snakes.”

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:44.910
There are plenty of other instances of Snakes
connected to Valak in The Nun.

00:04:44.910 --> 00:04:49.640
The throne thing occupied by The Mother Reverand,
who might I remind you ends up being Valak,

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:52.480
has an image embossed on it of two snakes
eating each other.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:56.130
When Father Burke chases the apparition of
Daniel into the graveyard during their night

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:59.580
at the abbey, snakes end up coming out of
Daniel’s mouth to attack him.

00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:03.000
Closer to the end of the movie, The Father
battles a figure with a serpent-like forked

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.000
tongue.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:07.240
And in the final battle against Valak, a snake
wraps itself around The Father’s neck and

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:10.520
bites him in the eye, which ties right back
into the book that the Father found after

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:14.390
being trapped in the coffin, which features
a single eye on the cover.

00:05:14.390 --> 00:05:18.090
There are two facets to the ending that I
want to talk about: one involving the manipulation

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:21.910
caused by Valak, and the other involving,
the true identity of Frenchie revealed in

00:05:21.910 --> 00:05:23.400
the very last scene.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:24.950
First let’s talk about Valak.

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:27.780
Before heading down into the depths of The
Abbey, the characters figure out that there

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:30.740
are no other nuns left, Valak has completely
taken over the place.

00:05:30.740 --> 00:05:34.190
It’s a little unclear if the people they
met in the beginning, such as The Mother Reverend

00:05:34.190 --> 00:05:38.740
and Sister Oana were alive at some point,
or if they were apparitions of Valak as well.

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:39.980
Here’s my answer.

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:44.320
The only real living human Nuns at the Abbey
are killed off in the prologue.

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:47.000
Everyone we see after that is a distortion
caused by Valak.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:05:50.240
Valak poses as The Mother Reverend and tells
Father Burke to stay the night because The

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:53.350
Nuns are currently taking a vow of silence
and cannot speak with them.

00:05:53.350 --> 00:05:55.360
This is a trap to get them locked inside the
Abbey.

00:05:55.360 --> 00:05:59.710
I mean, the vow of silence thing is kind of
true because they’re all dead.

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:03.910
When Frenchie discovers the body of Sister
Victoria, he mentions that he tried to contact

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:05.820
the Abbey but was unable to reach them.

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:08.300
This is because Sister Victoria was the last
Nun.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:11.960
We see the body of another one of The Nuns
fall out of a tree and land on him as he leaves

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:15.420
the Abbey, just one of many examples of The
Nun corpses throughout the area.

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:19.900
There’s also one confusing instance where
Irene talks to Sister Oana, but then discovers

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:21.310
her corpse moments later.

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:24.210
Then, Oana seems to be back alive in a following
scene.

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:27.910
The one she was really talking to is just
one of Valak’s tricks, but the body discovered

00:06:27.910 --> 00:06:31.620
under the sheets is the real Sister Oana,
who had died several weeks before.

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:35.740
There are many decapitation references that
could link to the death of each of these Nuns.

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:39.100
I already mentioned the one that fell from
the tree, there is also a statue in the main

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:42.330
hall area that the Father is studying in whose
head crumbles off.

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:45.960
When Frenchie saves Father Burke’s life,
he decapitates the zombie nun with an axe.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:49.930
You’ll also notice that many of the Nuns
that haunt the Father and Sister Irene are

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:52.680
faceless, as is the Jesus figure in the chapel.

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:55.700
Also in the end credits, there is some entity
with a burning head.

00:06:55.700 --> 00:07:00.200
The big reveal of this movie is actually foreshadowed
when we first meet Frenchy, as he is seen

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:01.560
at home feeding his goats.

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:05.660
Goats are an animal that are often used as
a symbol of demons and the devil, and the

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:09.270
French-Canadian farmer ends up being possessed
by Valak at the end of the movie.

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:12.990
In the epilogue, we discover his real name
is Maurice and he is the man receiving the

00:07:12.990 --> 00:07:18.230
exorcism in the clip Ed and Lorraine show
to their class way back in the original Conjuring.

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:19.620
“Take Maurice here.

00:07:19.620 --> 00:07:23.340
He’s a French-Canadian farmer, had nothing
more than a third grade education, but after

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:26.520
he was possessed, spoke some of the best Latin
I’d ever heard.

00:07:26.520 --> 00:07:27.520
Sometimes backwards.

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:33.220
A dark spirit made it’s home in this man.”

00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:42.250
“And like that, an upside-down cross started
to appear from within his body.”

00:07:42.250 --> 00:07:47.280
The big connection to Lorraine’s most feared
memory was five years in the making.

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:48.750
Did you see this twist coming?

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:49.750
Let me know if the comments.

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:54.130
Remember to like this video, and be back next
week as I’ll be discussing where the Conjuring

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:56.110
franchise will go from here.

00:07:56.110 --> 00:07:59.970
You definitely don’t want to miss out on
that, so be sure to subscribe to CZsWorld

00:07:59.970 --> 00:08:05.591
for new horrors every week, ring that deathbell
for notifications and I’ll see you in the

00:08:05.591 --> 00:08:06.610
next one.

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:08.800
Assuming we both survive.

